Stage: VR

Purpose:
  Verification stage. Owns final, whole-system verification of the unit
  of work after every other required stage has completed — confirming
  the original requirement is actually satisfied end-to-end, not just
  that each individual stage reported success.


Requires:
  Every required stage of the chain (see chains.sdd -> Completion), and
  DO when the unit of work required deployment.


Produces:
  Chain completion (see chains.sdd -> Completion — a chain is DONE only
  once VR has passed).


Important:
  VR is the final validation stage of a chain. VR MUST NOT be treated
  as an implementation stage (see chains.sdd -> Important — restated
  here since VR is this stage's own definition, not duplicated content).


Failure:
  A VR failure MUST trigger impact analysis before recovery, and
  recovery MUST re-run QA and DO before VR is attempted again (see
  chains.sdd -> VerificationFailure, Rules [C14]).


Optional:
  Never optional — see chains.sdd -> Rules [C11], chain completion
  requires VR to pass.


Skills:
  @../../skills/qa/

  (VR reuses the QA skill domain for verification technique — see
  chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn; this file defines WHEN/responsibility only,
  not HOW verification is actually performed.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/qa/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the VR responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  — every chain type ends here, per chains.sdd -> Rules [C11].
